table(["Disease", "Shipped model", "Accuracy", "Precision", "Recall", "F1", "ROC-AUC", "Predicted positive", "Majority baseline"], rows)
w("Findings: (1) on real data the algorithms score 76.5 % (diabetes), 84.3 % (heart), 71.8 % (liver), 97.6-98.8 % (kidney) - **much lower than the 88-92 % on synthetic data for diabetes, heart and liver**, as expected for noisy real clinical data; the kidney set is almost separable. (2) The shipped models transfer only partly: ROC-AUC 0.80 / 0.88 / 0.75 / 0.99 shows the *ranking* of risk carries over, but the 0.5 decision rule is badly calibrated for real populations - for liver the accuracy (54.0 %) is **below the 71.4 % majority-class baseline**. The application must not be used for real clinical decisions; the real-data numbers above are the more honest estimate of how this method behaves on patients. (3) Heart codes (cp, slope, thal) had to be mapped; the thal mapping is arbitrary.")
w()

